<http://data.silknow.org/object/1cd3a0af-fe98-3396-98e3-ce7bffaf836d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Complete sari of red silk with gold-wrapped thread designof squares and dots in the field. The deep gold pallu has border designs of floral motifs in tapestry weave in coloured silks."@en , "7. SARI\nSilk with gold-wrapped thread\nCentral India\n1850-1900\nIS.181-1960\n\nThis elaborate sari is 7.6 metres long. It would have been worn in the Central Indian style, as shown here, with one end of the fabric drawn between the legs and tucked into the waist at the back.\nThe other end has the decorative end-panel (pallu), which is meant to be displayed. The pallu is a deep panel of gold-wrapped thread. Its tapestry-woven borders are typical of the Central Indian or Paithani style of sari. [27/9/2013]"@en , "Sari of silk with gold-wrapped thread, Central India, 19th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c3da827c-1271-3022-a77e-4a6754bf2fa2> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/449be18f-5926-3c93-9991-3477c1076153> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6c22b25f-0200-3e0d-8c7d-8a834c739bed> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e970b846-77cb-31c8-9cbe-edae747f1ee6> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d74c6695-936a-3e07-a47e-63bdc46dfaa6> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d0b30da6-a1ea-301d-bde0-adb40bc6ee15> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1d022d58-a05e-33ba-b027-79fb55800988> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/27916961-fa9f-39d7-bad5-f68f12f8178c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "7. SARI\nSilk with gold-wrapped thread\nCentral India\n1850-1900\nIS.181-1960\n\nThis elaborate sari is 7.6 metres long. It would have been worn in the Central Indian style, as shown here, with one end of the fabric drawn between the legs and tucked into the waist at the back.\nThe other end has the decorative end-panel (pallu), which is meant to be displayed. The pallu is a deep panel of gold-wrapped thread. Its tapestry-woven borders are typical of the Central Indian or Paithani style of sari. [27/9/2013]"@en , "Sari of silk with gold-wrapped thread, Central India, 19th century"@en , "Complete sari of red silk with gold-wrapped thread designof squares and dots in the field. The deep gold pallu has border designs of floral motifs in tapestry weave in coloured silks."@en ;
